qualia:banksia_integrifolia
    tk:custodial_country "Bundjalung Country (Northern Rivers & Coastal Headlands NSW)" ,
                         "Gumbaynggirr Country (Mid-North Coast Headlands & Dunes NSW)" ,
                         "Worimi Country (Port Stephens & Stockton Bight Coastal Sands NSW)" ,
                         "Awabakal Country (Newcastle & Lake Macquarie Coast NSW)" ,
                         "Dharawal Country (Illawarra & Southern Sydney Coast NSW)" ,
                         "Yuin Country (South Coast Headlands, Estuaries & Dunes NSW)" ,
                         "Gunai / Kurnai Country (East Gippsland & Ninety Mile Beach VIC)" ,
                         "Bunurong Country (Western Port & Mornington Peninsula Coast VIC)" ,
                         "Wadawurrung Country (Bellarine & Surf Coast Littoral VIC)" ;
    tk:noticeType "TK_Notice_Open_To_Collaborate" , "BC_Notice_Biocultural_Provenance" ;
    tk:noticeRef <https://localcontexts.org/labels/traditional-knowledge-labels/> ;
    q42:commonsGovernance "Social Permissive Commons (SPC)" ;
    rdfs:comment "Country attribution spans Bundjalung, Gumbaynggirr, Worimi, Awabakal, Dharawal, Yuin, Gunai/Kurnai, Bunurong, and Wadawurrung Nations along South-Eastern Australian coastal dunes and headlands. Ethnographic records note soaking nectar-rich Banksia spikes in water for sweet seasonal drinks and using smouldering cones for carrying embers. Local Contexts TK/BC notices record biocultural provenance without asserting community-authored TK labels absent direct First Nations co-design."@en .
